  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 203 AM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nBy Tuesday morning, most of the rain will have cleared west Texas \nand southeast New Mexico as our area ends up behind the upper-level \ntrough. Diminished cloud cover and rising heights allow temperatures \nto climb back into the mid-to-upper 70s and low 80s through \nThursday. However, by Thursday our region once again ends up under \nsouthwesterly flow aloft. Shortwaves within this flow allow rain \nchances to increase yet again across the area, mainly Thursday \nafternoon into Friday. Increased cloud cover and rain chances keep \nhighs a bit cooler Friday (temperatures in the 70s for most \nlocations). Once again, it looks like PWATs will be in the 90th \npercentile or higher across the area, so heavy rainfall leading to \nat least localized flash flooding would be a concern. Still plenty \nof details to iron out, so stay tuned for updates! Rain chances look \nto diminish Saturday behind a weak Pacific front.\n\nSprang",
